<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janissaries</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as janissary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Janissaries were the elite infantry corps of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, originally recruited from Christian boys through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devshirme">devshirme</a> system. They became one of the first standing armies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> to use firearms on a large scale. Comparable slave-soldier corps were developed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>, and the Janissaries were abolished in 1826.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janissaries.jpg" alt="Janissaries" width="278" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lambert Wyts · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lambert_Wyts_-_Agha_of_the_Janissaries_and_a_B%C3%B6l%C3%BCk_of_the_Janissaries.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
